\f1\fs22 The Agora Symposium Bar and\cf3  Estiat\'f3rio \cf2 was exactly the kind of establishment that would make actual ancient Greeks regret  their influence on Western civilisation. Whitewashed arches divided the dining room into little courtyards, blue shutters decorated walls without windows, and an olive tree grew out of a brass pot between the toilets. Above the bar, Zeus threw lightning at the drinks specials board.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 Three men reclined on the overstuffed kline couches in the VIP section. They had booked the entire back room under the name, \'93Seven Sages I.K.E.\'94 A small fountain burbled in the centre, surrounded by platters of olives, feta and honey-drizzled figs that none of them had touched.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Kleo read a menu. \'93They have moussaka.\'94\
\'93And goat,\'94 Solo added, briefly impressed. \'93Oh. It comes with fries and thousand island dressing.\'94\
Chilo threw down his menu. \'93There\'92s a curry on the chef\'92s suggestions.\'94 He chewed on some dolm\'e1des. \'93What did they make these from? Gum leaves?\'94 He tossed the remnant to the table.\
Sounds approximating music filtered through form front-of-house. A band sounded like they were still arranging a tune for bouzoukis and an electronic drum kit. Kleo pined for the days when he could have had the musicians arrested. But he was a gentler man now. Sadder.
\f2\fs24 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \

\f1\fs22 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth0 Solo tore bread and dragged it through taramasalata. \'93Has anyone seen our missing socks?\'94 he mocked.\
\'93Filthy things,\'94 Chilo said. \'93Let your feet breathe. Wear sandals.\'94 Chilo inspected his toes and waggled his toes.\
\'93The message was surprising,\'94 Kleo agreed. \'93But at least they have something to chase now.\'94\
Chilo poured more retsina and offered the bottle to Kleo, who waved it away. Solo made a gimme-gimme gesture. Solo half-filled his glass and returned the bottle.\
\'93I\'92m concerned for Sarah,\'94 Kleo said and looked in the reflection in his wine.\
\'93The child is what matters.\'94 Chilo bit into another dolm\'e1des and pulled a face at it. \'93Two more sleeps until Christmas.\'94\
\'93Eloise seems to be on side,\'94 Solo said.\
Chilo laughed. \'93Eloise is on Eloise\'92s side.\'94\
\'93Good enough.\'94\
\'93Her engineers have met expectations,\'94 Solo said.\
\'93They have,\'94 Kleo added.\
\'93And Johnny will claim whatever idea we whisper in his ear.\'94 Chilo reached for the retsina again.\
Solo intercepted it.\
Chilo looked at his hand.\
Solo poured himself another half-glass. \
Chilo retrieved the bottle when Solo put it down, filled his glass raised it. \'93
\f3\i Zeus Soter
\f1\i0 !\'94\
The other two raised their glasses and drank.\
\'93
\f3\i Agathou Daimonos
\f1\i0 !\'94 Kleo toasted.\
The drank and replenished their glasses.\
\'93The washing machine!\'94 Solo toasted. \'93And to its next message.\'94\
\'93May it move in circles,\'94 Kleo said wearily.\
They feel quiet for a time.\
\'93What of the Fridge Force operative?\'94 Solo asked.\
The music out front sounded like the bouzoukis players had taken to keyboardist with the thick ends of their instruments.\
\'93None of us saw Sarah recruiting him,\'94 Kleo said, looking pained.\
Chilo looked unenthusiastically at the plates on the table. \'93I don\'92t like surprises.\'94\
\'93You like surprises you arranged,\'94 Solo said.\
Chilo smiled, but it didn\'92t reached his eyes. \'93Those are the best kind.\'94\
Kleo picked up one of the honeyed figs and turned it between his fingers. \'93Young Stockwell will take himself off the board sooner or later.\'94\
\'93It needs to be soon,\'94 Chilo observed.\
\'93Five seconds before time is time enough,\'94 Kleo said.\
Solo nodded. \'93He\'92s getting reckless.\'94\
\'93Don\'92t push that button: you\'92ll blow us all to skat\'e1,\'94 Chilo mocked.\
Even Kleo laughed.\
\'93That\'92s the espresso machine, Chip,\'94 Solo riffed.\
\'93But someone was making coffee at Rotherhithe!\'94 Chilo continued.\
Kleo was already tiring of the joke. He ate the fig.\
Chilo reached for another dolm\'e1des, considered it, and chose an olive instead.\
A waiter came through carrying three plates.\
\'93Goat, no dressing?\'94\
Solo raised his hand. A plate landed in front of him.\
Chilo had ordered the lamb, Kleo the fish.\
Solo cut into the goat. \'93What about Chanta?\'94\
Chilo chewed. Kleo tested a lemon wedge and squirted himself in the eye.\
Finally Chilo said, \'93What about him?\'94\
\'93I have no idea what he\'92ll do.\'94 Kleo aimed the lemon at the fish and got Solo in the eye.\
\'93I think he\'92s spent,\'94 Chilo said.\
\'93He\'92ll want to be at the birth,\'94 Kleo said.\
\'93Pacing around outside the door,\'94 Solo assessed.\
\'93Still,\'94 Chilo countered. \'93The Elvi may want to come get her before she goes into labour.\'94\
Kleo shrugged. \'93One way or another, Little Clinton will be born.\'94\
\'93The One After the One,\'94 Solo corrected.\
\'93Sarah calls him Little Clinton,\'94 Kleo rebutted.\
\'93Praise the Dawkins,\'94 Chilo saluted, always the most enthusiastic for the mission. Making prophecy happen was never so much fun.\
Solo said, \'93And Alexander?\'94\
All three went quiet.\
Then Kleo began laughing.\
Solo joined him.\
Chilo tried to hold out, failed, and lowered his head over his lamb.\
\'93Alexander,\'94 Kleo repeated.\
Chilo waved that away. \'93He\'92s too busy eating pork knuckle and getting European haircuts.\'94\
Kleo leaned back into the kline and laughed until he coughed. Solo slapped the couch. Chilo spilled retsina down the front of his robe and laughed harder because of it. Eventually Kleo wiped his eyes.\
Solo stopped smiling first.\
Chilo noticed. \'93What?\'94\
Solo chewed another mouthful of goat. \'93Johnny.\'94\
\'93Bah! He steals our ideas.\'94\
\'93We give them to him.\'94\
Solo looked at Chilo squarely. \'93Well, you do.\'94\
\'93And you don\'92t stop me.\'94\
\'93Brothers,\'94 Kleo interceded. \'93Let\'92s not bicker.\'94\
\'93No.\'94 Chilo grinned. \'93Let\'92s wrestle!\'94\
\'93Can we finish dining first?\'94 Kleo reasoned.\
Chilo shrugged. \'93Sure.\'94\
Kleo shook his head. \'93I knew we should have cut the wine.\'94
